---
description: Sealed systems, ARK, Slingshot — apply when touching vaults, receipts, exports, encryption.
globs: "**/*.{ark,ark.py,sanitize.py,receipt.py}"
alwaysApply: false
---

Slingshot Prep is local metadata sanitation on a copy plus a SHA-256 receipt. Not an anonymous drop.

ARK1 envelope (if `ark.py` is in the tree):

- `python3 app/ark.py seal FILE --pass PASS --out FILE.ark`
- `python3 app/ark.py inspect FILE.ark --pass PASS`
- `python3 app/ark.py phoenix FILE.ark --pass PASS --extract OUT`

Phoenix is authorized local re-seal (gen+1). It is not a remote payload and does not run when a stranger opens the blob.

Do not ARK-overwrite evidence originals that must keep byte-for-byte provenance. Seal a copy.

Do not log passphrases. Do not commit `.ark` keys or passphrase files.
